---
import DocLayout from "../layouts/DocLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import Table from "../components/Table.astro";
import Callout from "../components/Callout.astro";
---

<DocLayout title="Built-in components" description="Every component in the library, and the one design system they share.">
  <h1>Built-in components</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Twelve components, one visual language. They all resolve to the same tokens, the same radius
    scale, the same shadow ramp and the same transition timings.
  </p>

  <h2>The surfaces</h2>

  <h3>Tooltip</h3>

  <p>
    The anchored popover used for steps with a target. Non-modal: focus enters once, then Tab
    continues through the page.
  </p>

  <CodeBlock
    lang="js"
    code={`{ tourId: "home.cta", title: "Create", content: "Start here.", placement: "bottom" }`}
  />

  <h3>Modal</h3>

  <p>
    The centred dialog used for <code>placement: "center"</code>, <code>centered: true</code>,
    <code>intro</code> and <code>completion</code>. A real modal: focus is trapped while it is open
    and restored when it closes.
  </p>

  <CodeBlock
    lang="js"
    code={`createTour({
  tourId: "x",
  intro: {
    title: "Welcome to Acme",
    content: "A two-minute tour of the essentials.",
    icon: "sparkle",
    actions: [{ label: "Let's go", primary: true, onClick: () => {} }],
  },
  completion: {
    title: "You're all set",
    content: "You can replay this tour any time from Help.",
    icon: "check-circle",
  },
  steps: [/* … */],
});`}
  />

  <h2>The chrome</h2>

  <Table
    head={["Component", "Class", "Notes"]}
    rows={[
      ["Overlay", "<code>.tat-overlay</code>", "Click-through unless <code>closeOnOverlayClick</code>"],
      ["Spotlight", "<code>.tat-spotlight</code>", "<code>aria-hidden</code>; decorative"],
      ["Arrow", "<code>.tat-arrow</code>", "Hidden when the tooltip is centred"],
      ["Progress bar", "<code>.tat-progress__bar</code>", "<code>role=\"progressbar\"</code> with min/max/now"],
      ["Step counter", "<code>.tat-tooltip__counter</code>", "Enabled with <code>showStepCounter</code>"],
      ["Previous", "<code>.tat-btn--previous</code>", "Hidden on the first step"],
      ["Next / Done", "<code>.tat-btn--primary</code>", "Label and icon change on the last step"],
      ["Skip", "<code>.tat-btn--skip</code>", "Shown only when there is something after it"],
      ["Close", "<code>.tat-btn--icon</code>", "<code>showCloseButton</code>"],
      ["Custom actions", "<code>.tat-actions</code>", "From <code>step.actions</code>"],
      ["Live region", "<code>.tat-live</code>", "<code>role=\"status\"</code>, <code>aria-live=\"polite\"</code>"],
      ["Root", "<code>.tat-root</code>", "The single owned container"],
    ]}
  />

  <h2>Custom action buttons</h2>

  <CodeBlock
    lang="js"
    code={`{
  tourId: "home.cta",
  title: "Create a project",
  content: "Projects hold your dashboards.",
  actions: [
    { label: "Create one now", primary: true, onClick: () => openCreateModal() },
    { label: "Learn more", onClick: () => openDocs("#projects") },
  ],
}`}
  />

  <h2>Component gallery</h2>

  <div class="gallery" id="component-gallery">
    <p class="lede">Press Start to walk through each component in turn.</p>

    <div class="gallery__grid">
      <div class="gallery__demo" data-tour-id="gallery.panel">
        <strong>Anchored tooltip</strong>
        <span>Non-modal — Tab continues into the page.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="gallery__demo" data-tour-id="gallery.progress">
        <strong>Progress</strong>
        <span>Bar, counter and step dots share one style.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="gallery__demo" data-tour-id="gallery.actions">
        <strong>Custom actions</strong>
        <span>Rendered above the navigation controls.</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <button class="button button--primary" id="gallery-start">Start the gallery tour</button>
  </div>

  <Callout title="One design system, not twelve">
    <p>
      Spacing, radius, shadows, typography and motion all come from the same custom properties. If
      you override <code>--tat-radius-lg</code>, the tooltip, the modal and the welcome dialog all
      change together. That is the point.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <h2>Renaming classes</h2>

  <p>Add your own classes without forking or rewriting the stylesheet:</p>

  <CodeBlock
    lang="js"
    code={`createTour({
  tourId: "x",
  classes: {
    root: "my-product-tour",
    tooltip: "my-product-tour__panel",
    overlay: "my-product-tour__scrim",
  },
  steps: [/* … */],
});`}
  />

  <p>
    The library's own classes are always kept, so nothing breaks — your classes are merged
    alongside them.
  </p>

  <h2>Icons</h2>

  <p>
    Six local SVG icons ship with the library: <code>chevron-left</code>,
    <code>chevron-right</code>, <code>close</code>, <code>check</code>,
    <code>check-circle</code> and <code>sparkle</code>. No icon package is a dependency and nothing
    is fetched from a CDN. Every icon is <code>aria-hidden</code> — the accessible name belongs to
    the button that contains it.
  </p>
</DocLayout>

<script>
  /**
   * The gallery runs the real library against real targets on this page.
   */
  import { createTour } from "@take-a-tour/core";
  import "@take-a-tour/core/styles.css";

  const gallery = document.getElementById("component-gallery");
  if (gallery) {
    const steps = [
      {
        // Centred: a real modal dialog, focus trapped while open.
        title: "Centred modal",
        content: "Focus is trapped here and restored when the tour ends.",
        centered: true,
        icon: "sparkle",
      },
      {
        tourId: "gallery.panel",
        title: "Anchored tooltip",
        content: "Non-modal. Tab continues into the page once you have entered it.",
        placement: "right",
      },
      {
        tourId: "gallery.progress",
        title: "Progress indicator",
        content: "Enable showStepCounter to replace the bar with “Step 3 of 5”.",
        placement: "bottom",
      },
      {
        tourId: "gallery.actions",
        title: "Custom actions",
        content: "Buttons you define are rendered above the controls.",
        placement: "left",
        actions: [
          { label: "Nice", primary: true },
          { label: "Close the docs tab" },
        ],
      },
    ];

    let tour = null;

    gallery.querySelector("#gallery-start")?.addEventListener("click", () => {
      tour?.destroy();
      tour = createTour({
        tourId: "component-gallery",
        steps,
        showProgress: true,
        showStepCounter: true,
      });
      tour.start();
    });
  }
</script>

<style>
  .gallery {
    margin: 20px 0;
    padding: 24px;
    background: var(--bg-subtle);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  }

  .gallery__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(180px, 1fr));
    gap: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }

  .gallery__demo {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
    padding: 14px;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  }

  .gallery__demo span {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
</style>